# npm packs from files[] in package.json, which on npm >=7 is a true allowlist:
# dist/ being in .gitignore does NOT strip it. Verified on npm 10 by packing
# with and without this file — identical 122-file tarballs both times.
#
# So this is belt-and-braces, not the mechanism. It exists because npm 6 DID
# apply the .gitignore fallback over files[], and a publisher on an old npm
# would otherwise ship an empty installer. files[] is the real fix; the real
# protection is verifying the tarball (see MAINTAINERS.md).
node_modules/
*.log
